"Issue #815: separate boards must not need connections to each other.
KiCad merges nets with the same name, even if their numeric IDs differ.

CIRCUIT JSON INPUT
Boards: 9
Independent R1.pin2 -> C1.pin1 connections: 9
Each connection is already routed within its own board.

EXPORTED KICAD NETS
Numeric ID | Net name
1 | pcb_board_0/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
2 | pcb_board_1/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
3 | pcb_board_2/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
4 | pcb_board_3/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
5 | pcb_board_4/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
6 | pcb_board_5/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
7 | pcb_board_6/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
8 | pcb_board_7/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1
9 | pcb_board_8/.R1 > .pin2 to .C1 > .pin1

EXPECTED VS ACTUAL
Unique net names: expected 9, actual 9
Native KiCad DRC missing connections: expected 0, actual 0

PASS: KiCad does not request connections between the independent boards."
